## Resolution
Implemented and fail-closed in code.

### Changes
- `tools/run_llm_s3_s4_cache.py`
  - records `format_contract_ok` independently;
  - supports `raw` and `schema_constrained` arms;
  - OpenAI-compatible schema constraint uses `response_format=json_schema`;
  - Ollama schema constraint uses `format=<JSON schema>`;
  - invalid format is persisted instead of conflated with semantic failure;
  - semantic metrics are eligible only for contract-valid schema-constrained output;
  - model/provider/temperature/seed/latency/usage/raw-output SHA/upstream hashes recorded;
  - matching cached outputs are reused unless `--force` is supplied.
- `tools/compare_s3_s4.py`
  - refuses LLM results unless `format_contract_ok=true`, `semantic_metrics_eligible=true`, and mode is `schema_constrained`;
  - refuses non-reportable EC results;
  - fails on upstream hash mismatch.
- `tests/test_llm_output_contract.py`
  - validates candidate partition, unknown-ID rejection, and schema-constrained enforcement markers.

Raw output remains a separate capability record and is not used as the reportable semantic arm. No architecture/generalization claim is authorized from the 135M result alone.
